  loaded contract explicitly.
- Confirmed legacy simulator defaults and legacy `build_panel_evidence_v4` calls remain opt-in and
  unchanged when no transition contract is supplied.
- Confirmed source commit scope is exactly the three authorized files.

## Critical review follow-up: sealed-manifest path containment

The Critical issue in `task-5-review.md` was corrected in separate commit `8769fb7`
(`fix: contain optimizer provenance paths`), containing only `agent_loop.py`.
The V4 audit composition now treats authenticated `config.source_root` as the provenance boundary:

- relative manifest values are joined lexically to that root and any `..` component is rejected;
- absolute values must already be lexically contained by the root;
- the root and every selected component are inspected with `lstat()` before resolution;
- symlinks and Windows reparse points/junctions are rejected at the root, intermediate-directory,
  and leaf positions;
- missing components, non-directory intermediate components, and non-regular leaves are rejected;
  and
- only after that walk is the path strictly resolved, containment is rechecked, and the existing
  digest and transition-contract identity checks run.

These checks remain ahead of PIT bundle loading, candidate worker-factory construction, simulator
construction, hashing, and transition-contract loading. The prior exact-object transition wiring
and digest/identity checks are unchanged.

The hardened direct smoke used the real repository `core/pit_provenance.py` as the in-root regular
file and its byte-identical main-checkout counterpart as an outside duplicate-digest file. Results:

```text
{'valid_relative': True, 'dotdot': True, 'outside_absolute': True,
 'duplicate_digest_equal': True, 'outside_duplicate_rejected': True,
 'leaf_reparse': True, 'intermediate_reparse': True, 'exact_contract': True,
 'valid_v4': True, 'v4_dotdot_preflight': True, 'v4_outside_preflight': True,
 'v4_reparse_preflight': True,
 'calls': {'bundle': 1, 'simulator': 1, 'worker': 0}}
```

The single bundle/simulator call is the valid control. All traversal, outside-absolute, duplicate-
digest, and reparse cases left the counters unchanged; no candidate worker was constructed. Windows
denied creation of real test symlinks in this sandbox (`OSError`), so leaf and intermediate reparse
branches were additionally exercised by controlling the established `_has_reparse_point` boundary
against real existing path components.

